Integrated rate equation for first order reaction

k=\frac{2.303}{t} \log \frac{a}{(a-x)}

or

\begin{aligned}
\frac{k}{2.303} t & =\log \frac{a}{(a-x)} \\
& =\log a-\log (a-x)
\end{aligned}

or $\log (a-x)=-\frac{k}{2.303} t+\log a$
Thus, if $\log (a-x)$ values are plotted against time ' $t$ ' the graph obtained should be a straight line.
